+  - `site logs <run> -n 100000` reads the whole log (the default is the last 40 lines).
+  - Right before submitting, `site pick FA --jobs N` with N the jobs about to go: one pick covers N submissions
+    for 60 min.
+  - Ack an event with `site ack E<n> --note "<run id>: <what the log showed>"`.
+  - Never wait in the foreground (no sleep, no polling loop): a job's end opens an event for the next step.
 Final message, short, readable by someone who has forgotten this entry (CLAUDE.md 0e): first the question this step
 answers and why it was asked, then what you did, what you found (numbers) and what it changes, the figure files that show it (absolute paths of the
 .png, every result has one: the main session sends them to the user with the result), what you recorded, the next
